<resources>
    <!-- Minimal manifest theme for the brief window before Compose content
         is set — actual UI theming all happens via Compose's NextlayerTheme
         inside setContent {}. Extends a platform theme directly so this
         app doesn't need the classic (View-system) Material Components
         library as a dependency alongside Compose Material3.

         Dark parent + a near-black windowBackground (matching
         ui/theme/Color.kt's NlNearBlack) instead of the platform default
         white: the first thing most users see is the dark-branded Welcome
         screen, so a white flash before it would be the more jarring of
         the two trade-offs — no values-night variant for the inverse case
         since it's a sub-100ms window either way. -->
    <style name="Theme.Nextlayer3D" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#0A120D</item>
    </style>
</resources>
